asteroids A810: all IBs of a submission in one frame, one fence

UNTESTED on the phone, compiled with the build's flags only. Turnip's command stream continues across IBs when its BO fills. A frame per IB put a fence and CP_SET_THREAD_BOTH between the two halves, usually after the pass's CP_THREAD_CONTROL(BR | CONCURRENT_BIN_DISABLE) and before its IB2, so that pass's draws also ran on BV. 75 of 75 hung submissions with a history had two IBs, against 4 of the 525 submissions before them. Linux's a7xx_submit uses one frame. sweetibsplit=1 keeps the old framing for a control run. Each several-IB submission is logged, up to 64 a boot.

Apply: git apply in the kernel tree (-p1), after 2059 and 2063.

